commit 96f1e900c82af80b1316304ef069aad39ce4482b
Author:     Alexis Grigorev <alexis-ag@mail.ru>
AuthorDate: Thu Feb 12 14:05:02 2026 +0300
Commit:     Alexis Grigorev <alexis-ag@mail.ru>
CommitDate: Thu Feb 12 14:05:02 2026 +0300

    Add field alias compression study: research + article
    
    Three-part empirical study investigating whether field name abbreviations
    (aliases) save tokens in schema-once compact output. Finding: NO-GO.
    Aliases save a fixed 5 tokens (header-only) while schema() discovery
    costs 85 tokens per roundtrip — net loss in 75% of scenarios.
    
    Includes synthetic benchmarks, LLM comprehension tests (0% degradation
    with dictionary, per Columbo EMNLP 2025), session simulator, and
    workflow token budgets. Published as article in articles/.

