.research/260218_alternative_mutation_patterns.md:76:Independent execution (same as agentquery's existing read batches). Per-statement errors don't abort the batch. Transactional/saga patterns are too heavy for a CLI DSL — handlers can implement internally if needed.
.research/260218_alternative_mutation_patterns.md:80:None of the Go CQRS libraries provide runtime introspection — they rely on Go's type system. This is the gap that agentquery's `schema()` fills.
